DexSwapModule_Validate
├── when params are too short
│   └── it should return false with invalid params encoding
├── when target token is zero address
│   └── it should return false with zero target token
├── when target token equals sell token
│   └── it should return false with same input and output token
├── when amount is zero
│   └── it should return false with zero sell amount
├── when execution data provided with unwhitelisted router
│   └── it should return false with router not allowed
├── when execution data provided with zero min amount out
│   └── it should return false with zero min amount out
├── when execution data provided with expired deadline
│   └── it should return false with deadline expired
├── when caller has insufficient balance
│   └── it should return false with insufficient balance
├── when all valid without execution data
│   └── it should return true with empty reason
├── when all valid with execution data
│   └── it should return true with empty reason
├── validate and execute should agree on failure reasons (shared validator)
│   ├── it should agree on params too short
│   ├── it should agree on zero target token
│   ├── it should agree on zero sell amount
│   ├── it should agree on router not allowed
│   ├── it should agree on zero min amount out
│   ├── it should agree on deadline expired
│   ├── it should agree on insufficient balance
│   └── it should agree on same input and output token
└── fuzz: validate and execute agreement
    └── it should produce identical failure reasons for any amount and minAmountOut
